  "repeat": 1,
  "report": "**Conclusion: Supported.** In the United States, Kyleena (a levonorgestrel-releasing intrauterine system) is indicated/approved to prevent pregnancy for **up to five years**. The FDA-hosted prescribing-information label identifies Kyleena as a 19.5-mg levonorgestrel IUS, and the official labeling states that it is indicated for pregnancy prevention for up to five years; it should be replaced after five years if ongoing contraception is wanted. This directly supports the claim.\n\nSources:  \n- https://labeling.bayerhealthcare.com/html/products/pi/Kyleena_PI.pdf  \n- https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=2e07c155-21e1-4781-9633-ce8bddd47080  \n- https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/208224s005lbl.pdf",
